        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e19849af-cc5c-51ed-8f25-fe891f92a666",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Abraham Weinberg, George Weinberg, Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll, Dutch Schultz, Jack \"Legs\" Diamond, Salvatore Maranzano\n- Roles: mobster, gunman, mob accountant, hitman\n- Places: Manhattan, New York City\n- Events: Manhattan Bootleg Wars, gangland slayings\n\nFacts:\n- George Weinberg was born in 1901.\n- Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll, born Uinseann Ó Colla, was born on July 20, 1908.\n- During the 1920s and 1930s, George Weinberg was a New York mobster and, with his brother Abraham Weinberg, an associate of Dutch Schultz who worked as a mob accountant.\n- During the Manhattan Bootleg Wars, Abraham Weinberg became one of Dutch Schultz's top gunmen.\n- Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll was an Irish American mob hitman in New York City in the 1920s and early 1930s.\n- Abraham Weinberg was later a suspect in the gangland slayings of Jack \"Legs\" Diamond, Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll, and Salvatore Maranzano.\n- Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll died on February 7, 1932.\n- George Weinberg died on January 29, 1939.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
